  "result": "Perfect! All 88 tests pass. I've successfully implemented customer tier-based discounts. Here's what was added:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**src/customers.js**\n- Exported `TIER_DISCOUNTS` constant with discount percentages:\n  - `gold`: 5%\n  - `silver`: 2.5%\n  - `standard`: 0%\n\n**src/invoices.js**\n- **createInvoice**: Now applies customer's tier discount when a line has no explicit `discountPercent`. Explicit discounts (even 0) always override tier discounts.\n- **addLine**: For new lines, applies tier discount when no explicit `discountPercent` is provided. When updating existing lines, preserves the existing discount unless a new one is specified.\n\n**test/invoices.test.js**\n- Updated 5 existing tests to account for tier discounts being applied by default\n- Added 13 new tests covering:\n  - Tier discount application for each tier (gold 5%, silver 2.5%, standard 0%)\n  - Explicit discounts overriding tier discounts (including explicit 0)\n  - Mixed explicit and tier-based discounts in a single invoice\n  - Different tier discounts applied to different customer tiers\n  - Tier discounts applied when adding new lines with `addLine`\n  - Invoice totals calculated with tier-based discounts\n\nThe implementation ensures that tier discounts are consistently applied across all invoice creation paths while allowing explicit overrides on a per-line basis.",
